{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator clarification: fallback is configured on the three model classes, not per workflow. Direct Anthropic fallback should be enabled by configuring the Anthropic arm on each applicable class. The exact direct Anthropic Sonnet model has now been live-proven to support native structured output and thinking, so the earlier standard-class capability asymmetry can be resolved by recording that measured exact-ID capability; a general per-attempt workflow-routing redesign is not required for this symmetric fallback. The remaining implementation is class fallback configuration, pinned capability metadata, and a valid non-interactive credential. Heterogeneous future fallback pairs may still require separate per-attempt request-shaping work."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786330197768686001,"uuid":"70413e53-265d-4f49-b32e-09b83efb8c14"}